  "summary": "Preprints pair generative models with MD, enhanced sampling and latent-space analysis to resolve multimodal ensembles and rare transitions beyond single structures.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is treating biomolecular function as an ensemble problem, resolved by combining generative or predictive models with physics-based sampling. REVEAL chains generative secondary-structure sampling, trRosettaRNA2 prediction, unbiased MD and Markov state modeling for HIV-1 TAR RNA. Enhanced sampling resolves multimodal binding: funnel-restrained TAMD on Martini 3 with beta-VAE clustering for CYFIP1-eIF4E, and OneOPES for FCP1 binding Rap74, with a new free-energy decomposition. OriDynamics proposes a unified all-atom ensemble generator for monomers and complexes, while a transition-conditioned fingerprint ranks players within rare-event transition corridors. The sequence-design annealing paper is peripheral to this thread.",
